    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T00:19:48Z",
    "body": "Finding from the rework of PR #3790, and the decision on it.\n\n- The cause is in the part-parallel rings themselves. Where the offsets of two lobes first touch, the corner of ring j-1 is step/sin(a) from the corner of ring j, and a goes to 0. The disc of ring j does not reach that corner, so both flanks stay uncut. The flanks law is in `offset_pass_start/flanks.rs:62-91`.\n- This is on `main` now too. \"Pass starts at Inside\" on fig8 reads 10686 full-width points today, and no note names them.\n\nThe coordinator decided (the maintainer is away):\n1. PR #3790 names every full-width cut on the path by the flanks law, with a pin that asserts 0 unnamed cuts. This closes the silent part on `main` as well.\n2. PR #3790 also removes the cause: a cut along the cusp (the medial-axis branch) through the ring corners at a merge. The full-width count must be 0 for Outside, Auto and Inside on fig8.\n3. PR #3790 then also gets `Fixes #3788`.\n\nDropped:\n- The old Outside rings for the whole band. The band is one area, so this brings back the planner that #3744 removes.\n- A split along a seam. The ring pieces end in material, and the seam is cut full width.\n- Outside on the old set until this issue is fixed. This breaks the maintainer's rule that one ring set serves Auto, Inside and Outside.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
