    "created_at": "2026-11-24T00:48:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T00:48:40Z",
    "body": "Progress from PR #3790 (part (c), commit `2eb7b7214`):\n\n- `level_order::order` now uses the flanks law of the full-width meter (`level_flanks`). Both flank points, 0.9 tool radii either side of the walk, must stand in uncut material.\n- On fig8, Outside now names its waist cuts: \"Pass start Outside: 14 cut(s) take the full tool width ... the first is at X 45.442, Y 62.578\". That is the first place that the meter finds. Before, the narrow note was silent, and this was also the case on main.\n- Inside on fig8 reads 10686 meter points. The wall note names the cuts along the part wall. On main, no note named the other cuts at the waist. Now the narrow note names them (14 cuts).\n- Pins: `fig8_outside_offset_cuts_no_move_at_full_width` and `fig8_inside_offset_names_each_full_width_cut` (heavy).\n- Part (a), the cut along the cusp, is in work on the same PR.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
